<h2 id="decision">The Decision</h2>
<p>Vikings head coach Kevin O'Connell named Kyler Murray the team's starting quarterback for the 2026 season on Tuesday, August 11, ending a competition with J.J. McCarthy that had run through the spring and into training camp. Murray, the No. 1 overall pick in the 2019 draft, signed a one-year deal with Minnesota in March after being released by the Arizona Cardinals. He held the edge in practice reps throughout camp, including a larger share of full-team snaps, and the Vikings shut the competition down before the first preseason game.</p>
<p>McCarthy, the team's 2024 first-round pick, will serve as the backup. He missed his entire rookie season to a torn meniscus and was limited to 10 starts in 2025 due to a string of injuries, going 6-4 as a starter but posting a 72.6 passer rating with 12 interceptions against 11 touchdowns.</p>
