<h2 id="combine">The Combine Murray Skipped</h2>
<p>Murray's 2019 combine measurements made headlines before he ran a single drill: 5-foot-10⅛ and 207 pounds, three pounds heavier than Russell Wilson's combine weight in 2012, with a 9.5-inch hand size that eased concerns about his smaller frame. But Murray never ran the 40-yard dash, at the combine or at his Oklahoma pro day — he chose to focus exclusively on throwing, leaving evaluators without an official time on one of the sport's most electric athletes.</p>
<p>That absence of a number didn't stop teams from betting on his athleticism. Murray was CFB's most explosive dual-threat prospect in his 2018 Heisman-winning season at Oklahoma, rushing for 1,001 yards and 12 touchdowns to go with 4,361 passing yards and 42 touchdowns through the air — the kind of tape that made a missing 40 time almost irrelevant to his draft stock.</p>
