<h2 id="acl">The ACL Recovery</h2>
<p>Murray's athletic profile has already been tested by a major injury once before. His 2022 season ended in Week 14 with a torn ACL, keeping him off the field until November 2023 — a recovery timeline consistent with the layered return-to-play testing most NFL teams use for knee injuries. That comeback holds useful context for anyone tracking his move to Minnesota: teams don't clear a scrambling quarterback for full-speed play until strength symmetry, jump testing, and change-of-direction drills all clear specific thresholds, not just time on the calendar.</p>
