<h2 id="outlook">2026 Outlook</h2>
<p>Murray inherits one of the more talent-rich rosters of his career, with Justin Jefferson, Jordan Addison, and T.J. Hockenson at the skill positions and an offensive line considered among the league's better units. His last five seasons have included exactly one full 17-game slate, so durability remains the biggest swing factor for Minnesota's 2026 outlook — but on pure talent, this is the strongest supporting cast he's ever played behind.</p>
<h2 id="faq">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
<div class="faq-item">
<div class="faq-q">Why didn't Kyler Murray run the 40-yard dash at his combine?</div>
<div class="faq-a">Murray chose to focus exclusively on throwing at both the 2019 NFL Combine and his Oklahoma pro day, skipping the 40-yard dash and all other athletic testing drills. His draft stock was driven almost entirely by his college production and passing evaluation rather than measurable testing.</div>
</div>
<div class="faq-item">
<div class="faq-q">What happened to J.J. McCarthy after losing the QB competition?</div>
<div class="faq-a">McCarthy will serve as Kyler Murray's backup for the 2026 season. Reports have since surfaced questioning whether McCarthy might request a trade, though the Vikings have stated he remains an important part of the quarterback room.</div>
</div>
<div class="faq-item">
<div class="faq-q">How serious was Kyler Murray's 2022 ACL injury?</div>
<div class="faq-a">Murray tore his ACL in Week 14 of the 2022 season, ending his year early. He didn't return to the field until November 2023, a recovery timeline in line with typical NFL ACL rehabilitation windows of roughly 9 to 12 months.</div>
</div>
